-- title:
--   Over a Noetherian local ring $A$, a weakly $M$-regular sequence in the maximal ideal has length at most $\dim A/\mathfrak{p}$ for every associated prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of $M$
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$, $M$ a finitely generated $A$-module and $rs = (r_1, \dots, r_n)$ a weakly $M$-regular sequence of elements of $\mathfrak{m}$. Then $n \le \dim A/\mathfrak{p}$ for every associated prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of $M$. A list $r_1, \dots, r_n$ of elements of $A$ is weakly $M$-regular when each $r_i$ is a nonzerodivisor on $M/(r_1, \dots, r_{i-1})M$ (Mathlib's `IsWeaklyRegular`; the last quotient may be zero), and $M$-regular (`IsRegular`) when moreover $M/(r_1, \dots, r_n)M \ne 0$. For a list $ps$, $(ps)$ is the ideal generated by its entries and $|ps|$ its length. Krull dimensions take values in $\{-\infty\} \cup \mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$ and heights of prime ideals in $\mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$.
--
--   **Proof.** Induction on $n$; for $n = 0$, $A/\mathfrak{p}$ is a nonzero ring, of dimension at least $0$. Let $x = r_1$ and write $\mathfrak{p} = \operatorname{ann}(m)$ with $m \ne 0$. By Krull's intersection theorem there is a largest $j$ with $m \in x^j M$; writing $m = x^j m'$ gives $m' \notin xM$, and $\operatorname{ann}(m') = \mathfrak{p}$ because $x$ is $M$-regular. The class of $m'$ in $M/xM$ is nonzero, so it lies under an associated prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $M/xM$, with $\mathfrak{p} + (x) \subseteq \mathfrak{q}$, while $x \notin \mathfrak{p}$. Since $x$ is a nonzerodivisor of the domain $A/\mathfrak{p}$ and $A/\mathfrak{q}$ is a quotient of $(A/\mathfrak{p})/(x)$, $\dim A/\mathfrak{q} + 1 \le \dim A/\mathfrak{p}$; the induction hypothesis for $M/xM$, $r_2, \dots, r_n$ and $\mathfrak{q}$ gives $n - 1 \le \dim A/\mathfrak{q}$.
--
--   **Novelty.** Classical; routine formalisation.
-- source:
--   H. Matsumura, Commutative Ring Theory, Cambridge Studies in Advanced Mathematics 8, Cambridge University Press, Th. 17.2, in the form of regular sequences; compare W. Bruns and J. Herzog, Cohen–Macaulay Rings, Cambridge Studies in Advanced Mathematics 39, Cambridge University Press, Th. 2.1.2(a), the equality for Cohen–Macaulay modules. C1.2 of the Diaz modulus mission. Formal proof: Diaz modulus mission, 29 October 2026 (C. Perassi).

import Mathlib

namespace DiazModulus

theorem length_le_ringKrullDim_quotient_of_mem_associatedPrimes {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [IsLocalRing A] (rs : List A) {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module.Finite A M]
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M rs) (hmem : ∀ r ∈ rs, r ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (p : Ideal A) (hp : p ∈ associatedPrimes A M) :
    (rs.length : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ p) := by
  sorry

end DiazModulus
